// cwe_22_unfired.strata -- T-0145 per-CWE litmus, design-finding fixture:
// CWE-22 (Improper Limitation of a Pathname to a Restricted Directory,
// "Path Traversal") is cataloged with `capability_kind=None`
// (`_threat.py::CWE_CATALOG`'s own comment: "flow-to-filesystem-path-sink
// precondition, not a capability kind the charter's auto-instantiate
// table lists"). No `may` atom ANY node declares can ever drag this
// obligation in -- `_fired_obligations`/`_entries_by_capability_kind`
// only join entries whose `capability_kind is not None`
// (docs/strata/threat.md#the-litmus-coverage-cwe-22352798-never-fire-by-
// design). This fixture models the scenario a path-traversal weakness
// would actually look like (a foreign caller feeding a filesystem-facing
// node) precisely to prove the negative: even here, THREAT003 reports
// ZERO CWE-22 obligations, because the precondition the catalog would
// need to detect it structurally does not exist in phase A. No hardened
// twin: there is nothing to discharge when nothing fires.
//
// tested end to end (parse -> elaborate -> check_discharge_completeness)
// by tests/unit/strata/test_litmus_cwe.py, which asserts this NON-firing
// explicitly rather than skipping the id.

module cwe_22_unfired

node client : foreign { clearance Public; }
node file_server : trusted {
    clearance Internal;
}

flow f_read : client -> file_server { label Public; }
